<p class="dev-intro">Build a local MediaWiki environment with Docker Compose, then add the services you need.</p>

<div class="dev-paths">
  <a href="#getting-started"><strong>Getting started</strong><span>Create and install your first local wiki.</span></a>
  <a href="/manual/dev/mediawiki/"><strong>MediaWiki</strong><span>Work with checkouts, extensions and maintenance commands.</span></a>
  <a href="#services"><strong>Services</strong><span>Add databases, caches, debugging tools and more.</span></a>
  <a href="/manual/dev/env/"><strong>Environment configuration</strong><span>Inspect and change your environment settings.</span></a>
</div>

<h2 id="getting-started">Getting started</h2>
<p>Install Docker with Compose and make sure <code>docker info</code> works. Create MediaWiki, add MySQL, then install the wiki:</p>
<Code code={'mw dev mediawiki create\nmw dev mysql create\nmw dev mediawiki install --dbtype=mysql'} lang="sh" />
<p>The setup wizard lets you choose a checkout and local port. For a separate environment, use <code>--context NAME</code>.</p>
<p><a href="/guides/dev/setup/">Read the setup guide →</a></p>

<h2 id="services">Working with services</h2>
<p>Read the <a href="/guides/dev/services/">service workflow guide</a> for the shared patterns.</p>
<p>Choose a service in the sidebar for its overview and commands. Many services share <code>create</code>, <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>logs</code> and image configuration commands; each service's reference lists what it supports.</p>
<ul>
  <li><a href="/manual/dev/mysql/">MySQL</a> and <a href="/manual/dev/postgres/">PostgreSQL</a> for databases.</li>
  <li><a href="/manual/dev/redis/">Redis</a> and <a href="/manual/dev/memcached/">Memcached</a> for caching.</li>
  <li><a href="/manual/dev/jaeger/">Jaeger</a> and <a href="/manual/dev/mailhog/">MailHog</a> for debugging.</li>
  <li><a href="/manual/dev/traefik/">Traefik</a> for gateway access and service URLs.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="managing-your-environment">Managing your environment</h2>
<p>Use <a href="/manual/dev/stop/">stop</a> and <a href="/manual/dev/start/">start</a> to pause and resume containers, or <a href="/manual/dev/compose/">compose</a> to work directly with Docker Compose.</p>
<p>For repeatable setups, <a href="/manual/dev/recipe/">recipes</a> apply a YAML definition of an environment.</p>

